{
  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  "edition_id": "ASV1901",
  "book_code": "JOB",
  "chapter": 34,
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "JOB.34.1",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.34.1",
      "verse": 1,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Moreover Elihu answered and said,",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.34.2",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.34.2",
      "verse": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Hear my words, ye wise men;\nAnd give ear unto me, ye that have knowledge.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.34.3",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.34.3",
      "verse": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For the ear trieth words,\nAs the palate tasteth food.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.34.4",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.34.4",
      "verse": 4,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Let us choose for us that which is right:\nLet us know among ourselves what is good.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.34.5",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.34.5",
      "verse": 5,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For Job hath said, I am righteous,\nAnd God hath taken away my right:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.34.6",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.34.6",
      "verse": 6,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Notwithstanding my right I am ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "accounted",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " a liar;My wound is incurable, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "though I am",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " without transgression.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.34.7",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.34.7",
      "verse": 7,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "What man is like Job,\nWho drinketh up scoffing like water,",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.34.8",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.34.8",
      "verse": 8,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Who goeth in company with the workers of iniquity,\nAnd walketh with wicked men?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.34.9",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.34.9",
      "verse": 9,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For he hath said, It profiteth a man nothing\nThat he should delight himself with God.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.34.10",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.34.10",
      "verse": 10,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Therefore hearken unto me, ye men of understanding:\nFar be it from God, that he should do wickedness,\nAnd from the Almighty, that he should commit iniquity.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.34.11",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.34.11",
      "verse": 11,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For the work of a man will he render unto him,\nAnd cause every man to find according to his ways.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.34.12",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.34.12",
      "verse": 12,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Yea, of a surety, God will not do wickedly,\nNeither will the Almighty pervert justice.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.34.13",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.34.13",
      "verse": 13,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Who gave him a charge over the earth?\nOr who hath disposed the whole world?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.34.14",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.34.14",
      "verse": 14,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "If he set his heart upon himself,",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "If",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " he gather unto himself his spirit and his breath;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.34.15",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.34.15",
      "verse": 15,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "All flesh shall perish together,\nAnd man shall turn again unto dust.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.34.16",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.34.16",
      "verse": 16,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "If now ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "thou hast",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " understanding, hear this:\nHearken to the voice of my words.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.34.17",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.34.17",
      "verse": 17,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Shall even one that hateth justice govern?\nAnd wilt thou condemn him that is righteous ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "and",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " mighty?—",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.34.18",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.34.18",
      "verse": 18,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Him",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " that saith to a king, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "Thou art",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " vile,",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "Or",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " to nobles, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "Ye are",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " wicked;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.34.19",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.34.19",
      "verse": 19,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "That respecteth not the persons of princes,\nNor regardeth the rich more than the poor;\nFor they all are the work of his hands.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.34.20",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.34.20",
      "verse": 20,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "In a moment they die, even at midnight;\nThe people are shaken and pass away,\nAnd the mighty are taken away without hand.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.34.21",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.34.21",
      "verse": 21,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For his eyes are upon the ways of a man,\nAnd he seeth all his goings.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.34.22",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.34.22",
      "verse": 22,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "There is no darkness, nor thick gloom,\nWhere the workers of iniquity may hide themselves.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.34.23",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.34.23",
      "verse": 23,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For he needeth not further to consider a man,\nThat he should go before God in judgment.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.34.24",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.34.24",
      "verse": 24,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "He breaketh in pieces mighty men ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "in ways",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " past finding out,\nAnd setteth others in their stead.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.34.25",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.34.25",
      "verse": 25,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Therefore he taketh knowledge of their works;\nAnd he overturneth them in the night, so that they are destroyed.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.34.26",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.34.26",
      "verse": 26,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "He striketh them as wicked menIn the open sight of others;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.34.27",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.34.27",
      "verse": 27,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Because they turned aside from following him,\nAnd would not have regard in any of his ways:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.34.28",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.34.28",
      "verse": 28,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "So that they caused the cry of the poor to come unto him,\nAnd he heard the cry of the afflicted.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.34.29",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.34.29",
      "verse": 29,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "When he giveth quietness, who then can condemn?\nAnd when he hideth his face, who then can behold him?\nAlike whether ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "it be done",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " unto a nation, or unto a man:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.34.30",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.34.30",
      "verse": 30,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "That the godless man reign not,\nThat there be none to ensnare the people.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.34.31",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.34.31",
      "verse": 31,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For hath any said unto God,\nI have borne ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "chastisement",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ", I will not offend ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "any more",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ":",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.34.32",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.34.32",
      "verse": 32,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "That which I see not teach thou me:\nIf I have done iniquity, I will do it no more?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.34.33",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.34.33",
      "verse": 33,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Shall his recompense be as thou wilt, that thou refusest it?\nFor thou must choose, and not I:\nTherefore speak what thou knowest.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.34.34",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.34.34",
      "verse": 34,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Men of understanding will say unto me,\nYea, every wise man that heareth me:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.34.35",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.34.35",
      "verse": 35,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Job speaketh without knowledge,\nAnd his words are without wisdom.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.34.36",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.34.36",
      "verse": 36,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Would that Job were tried unto the end,\nBecause of his answering like wicked men.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.34.37",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.34.37",
      "verse": 37,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For he addeth rebellion unto his sin;\nHe clappeth his hands among us,\nAnd multiplieth his words against God.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    }
  ]
}
